abstract: >-
  Code, genome records, host profile, alignments and intermediate results
  required to reproduce every table and figure of a comparative genomic survey
  of the lysis and host-recognition modules of 22 lytic Staphylococcus aureus
  bacteriophages. The toolkit is a host-neutral engine plus a host profile:
  stages S1-S4 extract genome statistics, holin and receptor-binding protein
  calls, terminase sequences for phylogeny, and endolysin candidates for domain
  validation; S4b measures per-domain pairwise identity; S6 and S7 cover de novo
  tRNA prediction and host codon usage; S7b compares phage and host codon usage.
  This release contains the Staphylococcus aureus profile only.
keywords:
  - bacteriophage
  - Staphylococcus aureus
  - comparative genomics
  - endolysin
  - receptor-binding protein
  - terminase
  - codon usage
  - genome annotation
